    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated to the north of Bray on the periphery of the Wicklow/Dublin border, James Everett Park is well-established residential development that continues to be a popular choice amongst buyers. No. 39 is a well-presented three-bedroom end of terrace home enjoying a quiet position within the estate, while benefiting from excellent access to the many amenities Bray has to offer.\n\nInternally, the accommodation extends to approximately 85 sq. m and is arranged over two floors. Entering through a tiled front porch, the entrance hall provides understairs storage and laminate wood flooring, which continues into the living room located to the right of the hallway. This bright and welcoming room features fitted display units and a feature fireplace creating an attractive focal point. To the rear, the open-plan kitchen/dining room spans the full width of the property and incorporates tiled flooring, wooden cabinetry, an integrated double oven, and ample worktop space. The dining area benefits from excellent natural light through a large picture window overlooking the rear garden and features laminate wood flooring and an attractive open fireplace.\n\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms comprising a spacious double bedroom with built-in wardrobe, a twin bedroom, and a generous single bedroom. A fully tiled family bathroom off the landing completes the accommodation and is fitted with a bath and overhead shower attachment. \n\nExternally, to the front, a driveway behind black gates provides secure off-street parking, with a lawn positioned to one side. The private rear garden is accessed via a side passage or directly from the kitchen/dining room and is laid out in a combination of lawn, patio, and gravel areas, creating a practical and low-maintenance outdoor space. A paved pathway leads to a timber garden shed, providing useful additional storage. The garden offers an ideal balance of lawn and seating areas, perfect for outdoor dining, gardening, or family enjoyment.\n\nThe location is exceptionally convenient, with a host of amenities nearby including parks, supermarkets, recreational facilities, and Bray Main Street which is within comfortable walking distance. Bray Seafront and Promenade are also close by, offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars, and scenic coastal walks. A range of highly regarded primary and secondary schools are in the area, while commuters are well served by the N11/M50, DART, and frequent bus routes. The Luas at Bride's Glen is also easily accessible by private transport."
      },
